2026-06-01 14:36:49,865 | AGENT | Final proposal generated: # 1. Executive Summary
Nexus Engineering S.r.l., in partnership with EuroCloud Solutions S.A., LexIA GmbH, and GreenCompute S.r.l., proposes a comprehensive artificial intelligence (AI) solution to enhance the efficiency of administrative services for the City of Belval. Our solution, leveraging AI research and development expertise, aims to provide intelligent assistance tools for municipal agents, facilitating access to information, improving answer quality, and reducing processing times. We ensure strict compliance with regulatory requirements, including GDPR, and prioritize sustainability by utilizing low-carbon impact infrastructures.

# 2. Understanding of Requirements
The City of Belval seeks an AI solution to assist its municipal agents in their daily missions, aiming to improve administrative service efficiency and quality. The expected solution must integrate with existing practices, provide quick access to reliable information, help with drafting administrative content, assist in file instruction, and facilitate collaboration among agents. It must also comply with regulatory requirements such as GDPR, ensure explicability of recommendations, and maintain high availability without automated decisions.

# 3. Proposed Solution
Our proposed solution leverages a microservices-based architecture utilizing Docker, Kubernetes, and Helm for efficient deployment and management. We will host the solution on SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure within the EU, ensuring compliance with GDPR and sovereignty constraints. For AI components, we will fine-tune the Mistral 7B large language model using LoRA or QLoRA methods to adapt it to the City's administrative context. Our Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) capabilities will facilitate agents' access to reliable information.

To achieve response times lower than 2 seconds and ensure high availability (99.9%), we will optimize system performance with monitoring tools like Prometheus, Grafana, and ELK stack. API integration using REST, GraphQL, or SOAP will enable seamless interaction with existing systems such as civil status, town planning, EDM, and user directories.

For security and compliance, we adhere to GDPR requirements, utilizing anonymization tools like Microsoft Presidio and custom NER models for sensitive data protection. Access control standards include multi-factor authentication (MFA) and role-based access control (RBAC). Our incident response plan includes a Security Incident Response Team (SIRT) and playbooks for handling security incidents.

Our budget breakdown, ensuring an annual cost of exploitation compatible with the City's budgetary capacities, will be detailed. With a target gross margin percentage of 28%, we estimate potential revenue and project margins over the 4-year contract period, optimizing costs through efficient project management and resource allocation.

To address environmental constraints, our solution relies on green hosting providers like OVHcloud and Scaleway, using 100% renewable energy. We balance high availability with energy consumption by utilizing low-power standby modes and preferring quantized mid-size models for AI tasks.

# 4. Unaddressed Requirements
No requirements from the tender are explicitly unaddressed in our proposal, as we have integrated contributions from all specialized agents to cover technical, security, regulatory, budgetary, innovation, and sustainability aspects.

# 5. Conclusion
Nexus Engineering S.r.l., along with its partners, is committed to delivering an innovative AI solution that not only enhances the efficiency of administrative services for the City of Belval but also ensures strict compliance with regulatory requirements and prioritizes sustainability. Our comprehensive approach, combining technical expertise with a deep understanding of public administration needs, positions us as a strong candidate to successfully implement this project within the specified budget and timeframe.
